From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:12:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/30] Keep the fork as a patch stack on upstream release tags

The fork fell 765 commits behind upstream while it merged on its own
schedule. A linear stack on a release tag rebases with rerere, shows each
change with range-diff, and drops a commit when upstream takes it.

FORK.md gives the workflow and the patch register. hack/fork/fork.sh
prints the base and the series, checks the trailers, exports the stack
as patch files and replays it onto a new tag. The constitution now
requires the stack and the v1.0 check commands.

Fork-Topic: fork-meta
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
